1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,410
"We cannot rule out price increases."
That's not a warning from some small

2
00:00:03,460 --> 00:00:04,950
brand you've never heard of.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,870
That's Toyota the biggest car company
in Australia talking about its utes and

4
00:00:08,920 --> 00:00:11,230
four-wheel drives from 2027.

5
00:00:11,280 --> 00:00:14,790
In October 2026, Toyota
Australia's sales boss,

6
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:18,550
John Pappas, said the new emissions
targets for utes and vans that kick in

7
00:00:18,600 --> 00:00:21,310
from 2027 are "really challenging".

8
00:00:21,360 --> 00:00:24,770
And when a company that sells tens of
thousands of HiLuxes and LandCruisers a

9
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:27,270
year says it can't rule out price rises,

10
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:31,130
every tradie, farmer and family with
a caravan should be paying attention.

11
00:00:31,180 --> 00:00:33,210
Because this isn't just about Toyota.

12
00:00:33,260 --> 00:00:37,777
The rules that start biting in 2027
apply to every ute brand in the country

13
00:00:37,827 --> 00:00:42,950
Ford, Isuzu, Mitsubishi,
Nissan, Mazda, GWM, all of them.

14
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:43,930
So in this video,

15
00:00:43,980 --> 00:00:46,870
I'll explain exactly what changes in 2027,

16
00:00:46,920 --> 00:00:49,510
why the diesel ute is suddenly
in the government's sights,

17
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:51,790
how much it could add to
the price of your next ute,

18
00:00:51,840 --> 00:00:53,690
which brands are best and worst placed,

19
00:00:53,740 --> 00:00:55,410
what the politicians are fighting about,

20
00:00:55,460 --> 00:00:58,510
and what it all means if you're
planning to buy a ute in the next twelve

21
00:00:58,560 --> 00:00:59,410
months.

22
00:00:59,460 --> 00:01:02,560
Stay with me, because the numbers
are bigger than most people realise.

23
00:01:03,199 --> 00:01:06,349
First, let's understand the
rule that's causing all of this.

24
00:01:06,399 --> 00:01:10,169
It's called the New Vehicle
Efficiency Standard, or NVES.

25
00:01:10,219 --> 00:01:13,069
It started on the 1st of January 2025,

26
00:01:13,119 --> 00:01:18,089
and car makers began earning credits
and penalties from the 1st of July 2025.

27
00:01:18,139 --> 00:01:19,449
The idea is simple.

28
00:01:19,499 --> 00:01:23,289
Every car brand gets an average carbon
dioxide target for all the vehicles it

29
00:01:23,339 --> 00:01:25,249
sells in Australia each year.

30
00:01:25,299 --> 00:01:27,689
Sell cleaner cars, and you earn credits.

31
00:01:27,739 --> 00:01:29,709
Sell dirtier ones, and
you build up penalties.

32
00:01:29,759 --> 00:01:31,669
There are two separate targets.

33
00:01:31,719 --> 00:01:34,229
One for passenger cars and SUVs.

34
00:01:34,279 --> 00:01:37,669
And a different one for light
commercial vehicles that means utes,

35
00:01:37,719 --> 00:01:40,169
vans and some big four-wheel drives.

36
00:01:40,219 --> 00:01:43,969
And here's the key part: the targets
get tougher every single year.

37
00:01:44,019 --> 00:01:45,049
For passenger cars,

38
00:01:45,099 --> 00:01:50,429
the target is 117 grams of carbon
dioxide per kilometre in 2026.

39
00:01:50,479 --> 00:01:52,929
In 2027 it drops to 92.

40
00:01:52,979 --> 00:01:56,729
Then 68 in 2028, and 58 in 2029.

41
00:01:56,779 --> 00:02:02,529
For utes and vans, the target is
180 grams per kilometre in 2026.

42
00:02:02,579 --> 00:02:05,449
In 2027, it drops to 150.

43
00:02:05,499 --> 00:02:08,229
Then 122 in 2028.

44
00:02:08,279 --> 00:02:10,669
And 110 in 2029.

45
00:02:10,719 --> 00:02:15,329
That jump from 180 to 150 is
the one Toyota is worried about.

46
00:02:15,379 --> 00:02:18,589
It's a cut of about seventeen
per cent in just one year.

47
00:02:18,639 --> 00:02:22,769
And the vast majority of utes sold in
Australia are diesel which means most of

48
00:02:22,819 --> 00:02:24,089
them are well above that line.

49
00:02:24,139 --> 00:02:25,489
As Pappas put it:

50
00:02:25,539 --> 00:02:29,149
"The big challenge comes from 2027
when it comes to light commercial

51
00:02:29,199 --> 00:02:31,509
vehicles." And timing matters here.

52
00:02:31,559 --> 00:02:36,509
The law requires a review of the
NVES to begin before the end of 2026.

53
00:02:36,559 --> 00:02:39,109
The current targets run through to 2029,

54
00:02:39,159 --> 00:02:42,489
and that review will help decide what
happens after that and whether anything

55
00:02:42,539 --> 00:02:43,989
changes along the way.

56
00:02:44,039 --> 00:02:47,339
So the next twelve months are when the
future of these rules gets decided.

57
00:02:48,089 --> 00:02:50,119
So how does the penalty actually work?

58
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:53,949
Roughly speaking, a car maker pays
about fifty dollars for every gram per

59
00:02:53,999 --> 00:02:57,559
kilometre a vehicle is over the
target, for every vehicle it sells.

60
00:02:57,609 --> 00:02:59,539
The real formula is more complicated,

61
00:02:59,589 --> 00:03:01,739
because it's based on
the brand's whole fleet,

62
00:03:01,789 --> 00:03:05,139
and cleaner vehicles can earn
credits to offset dirtier ones.

63
00:03:05,189 --> 00:03:08,059
But fifty dollars per gram
is the number to remember.

64
00:03:08,109 --> 00:03:09,419
Let's take a real example.

65
00:03:09,469 --> 00:03:14,979
CarsGuide reports that the HiLux SR5
with Toyota's V-Active mild hybrid diesel

66
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:18,059
is claimed at 191 grams per kilometre.

67
00:03:18,109 --> 00:03:21,379
That's already above
the 2026 limit of 180.

68
00:03:21,429 --> 00:03:26,639
CarsGuide estimated the penalty for
a HiLux like that at around $550 per

69
00:03:26,689 --> 00:03:28,659
vehicle in 2026.

70
00:03:28,709 --> 00:03:32,419
Now, here's a rough calculation of
my own and it's only an illustration,

71
00:03:32,469 --> 00:03:33,739
not an official figure.

72
00:03:33,789 --> 00:03:37,119
In 2027, the limit drops to 150.

73
00:03:37,169 --> 00:03:41,159
A ute at 191 grams would
then be 41 grams over.

74
00:03:41,209 --> 00:03:42,979
At fifty dollars a gram,

75
00:03:43,029 --> 00:03:46,539
that's around two thousand dollars
per vehicle, before any credits.

76
00:03:46,589 --> 00:03:49,719
And by 2029, when the target is 110,

77
00:03:49,769 --> 00:03:53,719
the same ute would be about eighty grams
over roughly four thousand dollars.

78
00:03:53,769 --> 00:03:58,519
In January 2026, carsales ran its
own theoretical numbers for Ford.

79
00:03:58,569 --> 00:04:02,339
It estimated the combined penalty for
the Ranger and Everest could work out at

80
00:04:02,389 --> 00:04:07,899
around $3,706 per vehicle if it was
passed straight on to buyers and that

81
00:04:07,949 --> 00:04:12,559
Ford's total theoretical bill could be
well over a billion dollars by 2029 if

82
00:04:12,609 --> 00:04:14,209
its sales mix didn't change.

83
00:04:14,259 --> 00:04:16,739
Carsales was clear that
these were assumptions,

84
00:04:16,789 --> 00:04:19,979
not predictions, because car
makers will change what they sell.

85
00:04:20,029 --> 00:04:21,829
But it shows the scale of the problem.

86
00:04:22,572 --> 00:04:23,542
So who pays?

87
00:04:23,592 --> 00:04:24,922
That's the big question.

88
00:04:24,972 --> 00:04:26,322
Think of it like a seesaw.

89
00:04:26,372 --> 00:04:30,962
On one side, every vehicle a brand sells
that's below the target adds credits.

90
00:04:31,012 --> 00:04:34,682
On the other side, every vehicle
above the target adds penalties.

91
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:38,522
A brand that sells lots of hybrids and
EVs can balance out a lot of diesel

92
00:04:38,572 --> 00:04:39,362
utes.

93
00:04:39,412 --> 00:04:42,782
A brand that sells almost nothing but
diesel utes has nothing on the other

94
00:04:42,832 --> 00:04:43,742
side of the seesaw.

95
00:04:43,792 --> 00:04:45,722
Car makers have a few options.

96
00:04:45,772 --> 00:04:49,162
They can sell more hybrids and
electric vehicles to earn credits.

97
00:04:49,212 --> 00:04:51,462
They can buy credits from other
brands that have too many.

98
00:04:51,512 --> 00:04:55,202
Or they can pay the penalty and
potentially pass some of that cost on to

99
00:04:55,252 --> 00:04:55,962
buyers.

100
00:04:56,012 --> 00:04:58,322
We already know who's
ahead and who's behind.

101
00:04:58,372 --> 00:05:02,022
In February 2026, NRMA
reported the first results,

102
00:05:02,072 --> 00:05:04,382
for the second half of 2025.

103
00:05:04,432 --> 00:05:05,702
On the penalty side,

104
00:05:05,752 --> 00:05:09,222
Mazda's liability was
around $25.4 million,

105
00:05:09,272 --> 00:05:11,782
Nissan's around $10.7 million,

106
00:05:11,832 --> 00:05:16,282
Subaru's almost $7 million and
Hyundai's about $4.2 million.

107
00:05:16,332 --> 00:05:17,622
On the credit side,

108
00:05:17,672 --> 00:05:19,422
BYD had more than six million credits,

109
00:05:19,472 --> 00:05:24,262
Toyota nearly 2.9 million and
Tesla more than 2.2 million.

110
00:05:24,312 --> 00:05:26,202
Toyota is in an interesting position.

111
00:05:26,252 --> 00:05:27,682
Overall, it's earning credits,

112
00:05:27,732 --> 00:05:31,382
thanks to all those hybrid
RAV4s, Corollas and Camrys.

113
00:05:31,432 --> 00:05:34,542
But its utes and big four-wheel
drives are a different story.

114
00:05:34,592 --> 00:05:36,642
And under the 2027 targets,

115
00:05:36,692 --> 00:05:39,982
even Toyota's hybrid success may not
be enough to cover the gap on the

116
00:05:40,032 --> 00:05:40,942
commercial side.

117
00:05:40,992 --> 00:05:44,962
That's why Pappas said Toyota hasn't
ruled out buying credits from rivals but

118
00:05:45,012 --> 00:05:47,842
that the company wants to be
"self-managed as much as possible".

119
00:05:47,892 --> 00:05:52,622
And it's why Toyota says it will use
the government's review of the NVES to

120
00:05:52,672 --> 00:05:55,352
push for what it calls a
more "pragmatic" ute target.

121
00:05:55,402 --> 00:05:57,262
And Toyota isn't alone.

122
00:05:57,312 --> 00:05:58,292
According to CarExpert,

123
00:05:58,342 --> 00:06:02,762
the NVES has already contributed to price
increases on the Ford Ranger and the

124
00:06:02,812 --> 00:06:04,282
petrol Ford Mustang.

125
00:06:04,332 --> 00:06:09,302
And Mazda, Isuzu and Ram have also
warned of higher prices under the scheme.

126
00:06:09,352 --> 00:06:11,602
Isuzu is in a particularly tough spot.

127
00:06:11,652 --> 00:06:14,782
Its whole local range is
the diesel D-Max and MU-X.

128
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:18,982
Back in 2025, Isuzu's
Australian managing director,

129
00:06:19,032 --> 00:06:22,222
Junta Matsui, said the company
would find a way to survive,

130
00:06:22,272 --> 00:06:26,042
balancing what Australians need from
a vehicle with the emissions targets.

131
00:06:26,092 --> 00:06:30,602
Isuzu has studied a mild hybrid, a
smaller diesel and an electric version.

132
00:06:30,652 --> 00:06:31,982
But in 2026,

133
00:06:32,032 --> 00:06:35,162
it cancelled its plans to bring
the electric D-Max to Australia,

134
00:06:35,212 --> 00:06:37,682
with Isuzu's Rod Caldwell saying simply:

135
00:06:37,732 --> 00:06:40,702
"Customers don't want it."
One more thing worth knowing:

136
00:06:40,752 --> 00:06:42,302
the first actual penalty bills,

137
00:06:42,352 --> 00:06:47,452
for vehicles sold in 2025, aren't due
to be determined until February 2028.

138
00:06:47,502 --> 00:06:50,402
Car makers have time to
trade credits before then.

139
00:06:50,452 --> 00:06:53,712
So nobody knows yet exactly how
much will be passed on to buyers.

140
00:06:54,649 --> 00:06:57,359
There's another change on the way
that could affect some of Australia's

141
00:06:57,409 --> 00:06:58,879
toughest vehicles.

142
00:06:58,929 --> 00:06:59,666
According to CarsGuide,

143
00:06:59,716 --> 00:07:04,399
a draft change could bring vehicles
with a gross vehicle mass between 3,500

144
00:07:04,449 --> 00:07:11,439
and 3,855 kilograms into the
NVES from the 1st of July 2027.

145
00:07:11,489 --> 00:07:14,499
Right now, heavier vehicles
sit outside the scheme.

146
00:07:14,549 --> 00:07:15,559
Why does that matter?

147
00:07:15,609 --> 00:07:19,109
Because some popular heavy-duty
vehicles sit right in that band.

148
00:07:19,159 --> 00:07:22,019
CarsGuide named the LandCruiser 70 Series,

149
00:07:22,069 --> 00:07:24,839
with a GVM of 3,510 kilograms,

150
00:07:24,889 --> 00:07:29,459
and the Toyota Tundra, at 3,536 kilograms.

151
00:07:29,509 --> 00:07:32,659
Both would be pulled into the emissions
scheme if that draft change goes

152
00:07:32,709 --> 00:07:33,279
ahead.

153
00:07:33,329 --> 00:07:35,539
And this fight over utes isn't new.

154
00:07:35,589 --> 00:07:39,099
Back in 2024, before the NVES became law,

155
00:07:39,149 --> 00:07:42,719
the Housing Industry Association warned
that "applying stringent efficiency

156
00:07:42,769 --> 00:07:46,599
standards with harsh penalties will
substantially drive up the price" of utes

157
00:07:46,649 --> 00:07:47,539
and vans.

158
00:07:47,589 --> 00:07:48,539
At the time,

159
00:07:48,589 --> 00:07:51,939
the government's consultation paper
claimed compliance would cost manufacturers

160
00:07:51,989 --> 00:07:55,059
about $190 per ute or van.

161
00:07:55,109 --> 00:07:58,459
Two years later, we're about to find
out who was closer to the truth.

162
00:07:58,509 --> 00:07:59,739
It's still a draft.

163
00:07:59,789 --> 00:08:00,839
But if you're a farmer,

164
00:08:00,889 --> 00:08:04,419
a miner or a serious tourer
looking at a LandCruiser 70,

165
00:08:04,469 --> 00:08:06,989
it's something to keep an eye on in 2027.

166
00:08:07,849 --> 00:08:10,619
Quick pause before we look
at what you can actually buy.

167
00:08:10,669 --> 00:08:12,179
Do you drive a diesel ute?

168
00:08:12,229 --> 00:08:15,799
Would you switch to a hybrid or electric
ute if the price was right or would

169
00:08:15,849 --> 00:08:17,159
you never give up diesel?

170
00:08:17,209 --> 00:08:18,279
Tell me in the comments.

171
00:08:18,329 --> 00:08:19,359
I read them all.

172
00:08:19,409 --> 00:08:20,379
And if you want honest,

173
00:08:20,429 --> 00:08:24,199
fact-checked videos about what's
coming for Aussie drivers in 2027,

174
00:08:24,249 --> 00:08:25,119
hit subscribe.

175
00:08:25,169 --> 00:08:26,829
It's free and it really helps.

176
00:08:27,598 --> 00:08:29,608
So how big is the diesel ute problem?

177
00:08:29,658 --> 00:08:30,638
Let's look at the numbers.

178
00:08:30,688 --> 00:08:35,155
According to September 2026
sales data reported by carsales,

179
00:08:35,205 --> 00:08:41,428
Australians bought 184,328 light commercial
vehicles in the first nine months

180
00:08:41,478 --> 00:08:42,988
of 2026.

181
00:08:43,038 --> 00:08:47,208
155,040 of them were diesel
that's about eighty-four per cent.

182
00:08:47,258 --> 00:08:49,048
Electric light commercials?

183
00:08:49,098 --> 00:08:51,168
Just 1,630.

184
00:08:51,218 --> 00:08:53,628
The 4x4 ute market is also shrinking.

185
00:08:53,678 --> 00:08:58,388
It was down 13.6 per
cent, to 140,410 sales.

186
00:08:58,438 --> 00:09:02,988
The Ford Ranger 4x4 led with 35,744,

187
00:09:03,038 --> 00:09:07,928
ahead of the HiLux 4x4 on 32,238,

188
00:09:07,978 --> 00:09:09,548
which was down 6.2 per cent.

189
00:09:09,598 --> 00:09:12,548
And Toyota points out who's
buying these vehicles.

190
00:09:12,598 --> 00:09:16,308
Nearly fifty-four per cent of HiLux and
LandCruiser buyers live outside major

191
00:09:16,358 --> 00:09:17,248
cities.

192
00:09:17,298 --> 00:09:19,728
Pappas argues that for
regional and rural Australians,

193
00:09:19,778 --> 00:09:22,128
with long distances and limited charging,

194
00:09:22,178 --> 00:09:24,768
diesel is still the practical choice.

195
00:09:24,818 --> 00:09:27,638
That's the heart of Toyota's
argument for a softer target.

196
00:09:27,688 --> 00:09:29,988
Meanwhile, the wider
market is changing fast.

197
00:09:30,038 --> 00:09:33,908
The Australian Automobile Association
reported that battery electric and

198
00:09:33,958 --> 00:09:39,048
plug-in hybrid vehicles made up 31.61
per cent of new light vehicle sales in

199
00:09:39,098 --> 00:09:44,988
the June quarter of 2026 up from
19.07 per cent in the March quarter.

200
00:09:45,038 --> 00:09:47,168
Passenger cars are going electric quickly.

201
00:09:47,218 --> 00:09:51,248
In fact, CarExpert reported that
electric vehicles outsold both petrol and

202
00:09:51,298 --> 00:09:54,908
diesel vehicles in August
and September 2026.

203
00:09:54,958 --> 00:09:57,868
Utes are the part of the
market that's furthest behind.

204
00:09:57,918 --> 00:09:59,248
To be fair to Toyota,

205
00:09:59,298 --> 00:10:03,368
it says it supports the NVES and
wants it to be "fair and equitable".

206
00:10:03,418 --> 00:10:06,468
It points out it has spent more
than twenty years selling hybrids,

207
00:10:06,518 --> 00:10:09,948
and that its strategy is what
it calls "multi-pathway" hybrid,

208
00:10:09,998 --> 00:10:14,448
petrol, diesel, electric and eventually
hydrogen, depending on the market.

209
00:10:14,498 --> 00:10:18,008
Pappas described diesel as "the right
tool of trade for regional and rural

210
00:10:18,058 --> 00:10:18,448
Australia".

211
00:10:18,498 --> 00:10:21,508
The argument isn't really
about whether to cut emissions.

212
00:10:21,558 --> 00:10:24,318
It's about how fast utes
can realistically get there.

213
00:10:25,028 --> 00:10:26,518
So what are the alternatives?

214
00:10:26,568 --> 00:10:30,098
If diesel utes get more
expensive, what else is there?

215
00:10:30,148 --> 00:10:35,138
In May 2026, CarExpert listed every
electrified ute on sale in Australia.

216
00:10:35,188 --> 00:10:38,498
The cheapest was the GWM
Cannon Alpha plug-in hybrid,

217
00:10:38,548 --> 00:10:43,298
from around $57,490
drive-away in New South Wales.

218
00:10:43,348 --> 00:10:47,018
Then the Ford Ranger plug-in
hybrid from around $59,000.

219
00:10:47,068 --> 00:10:50,718
The KGM Musso EV from around $60,000.

220
00:10:50,768 --> 00:10:55,178
The BYD Shark 6 from around $62,660.

221
00:10:55,228 --> 00:11:00,238
The Deepal E07 electric
from around $70,137.

222
00:11:00,288 --> 00:11:04,898
And the Toyota HiLux
electric from around $82,752.

223
00:11:04,948 --> 00:11:08,298
The fuel crisis has changed
the maths for a lot of buyers.

224
00:11:08,348 --> 00:11:09,938
In May 2026,

225
00:11:09,988 --> 00:11:14,238
diesel reached as high as $3.50 a
litre in some parts of Australia,

226
00:11:14,288 --> 00:11:15,098
according to CarExpert.

227
00:11:15,148 --> 00:11:19,558
Filling an 80-litre Ranger
tank could cost up to $280.

228
00:11:19,608 --> 00:11:23,458
Ford cut the price of the Ranger plug-in
hybrid by up to ten thousand dollars,

229
00:11:23,508 --> 00:11:28,298
and the Wildtrak hybrid dropped to
$70,000 drive-away and dealer stock was

230
00:11:28,348 --> 00:11:30,978
soon "all but exhausted",
according to Ford.

231
00:11:31,028 --> 00:11:32,718
As a Ford spokesperson put it:

232
00:11:32,768 --> 00:11:36,538
"Australian buyers are doing the
maths." And a price war has started in

233
00:11:36,588 --> 00:11:37,958
plug-in hybrid utes.

234
00:11:38,008 --> 00:11:39,578
In May 2026,

235
00:11:39,628 --> 00:11:43,378
CarsGuide reported that Ford had cut
older Ranger plug-in hybrids to a

236
00:11:43,428 --> 00:11:50,038
recommended $62,000 drive-away,
down from a $71,990 sticker price.

237
00:11:50,088 --> 00:11:53,946
The new JAC Hunter plug-in hybrid was
targeting less than fifty thousand

238
00:11:53,996 --> 00:11:54,818
dollars drive-away.

239
00:11:54,868 --> 00:12:01,458
And Toyota's own 48-volt mild hybrid
diesel HiLux starts from $57,990 before

240
00:12:01,508 --> 00:12:03,098
on-road costs.

241
00:12:03,148 --> 00:12:04,038
More are on the way.

242
00:12:04,088 --> 00:12:07,898
Chery has a diesel-electric
ute due before the end of 2026,

243
00:12:07,948 --> 00:12:11,438
with a petrol-electric
version expected in 2027.

244
00:12:11,488 --> 00:12:15,178
GWM plans a plug-in hybrid
version of its smaller Cannon ute.

245
00:12:15,228 --> 00:12:19,478
And Nissan's next-generation Navara is
set to use Mitsubishi's plug-in hybrid

246
00:12:19,528 --> 00:12:20,498
technology.

247
00:12:20,548 --> 00:12:25,258
By 2027, ute buyers will have more
electrified choices than ever before.

248
00:12:25,308 --> 00:12:27,598
And Toyota itself sells an electric HiLux,

249
00:12:27,648 --> 00:12:33,698
from $74,990 to $82,990 before on-road

250
00:12:33,748 --> 00:12:34,158
costs.

251
00:12:34,208 --> 00:12:41,198
For comparison, the diesel HiLux
4x4 range runs from $45,990 to

252
00:12:41,248 --> 00:12:44,718
$71,990 before on-road costs.

253
00:12:44,768 --> 00:12:48,178
So right now, the electric version
is still a lot more expensive.

254
00:12:48,228 --> 00:12:50,098
That's the squeeze in a nutshell.

255
00:12:50,148 --> 00:12:52,518
Diesel utes face rising penalties.

256
00:12:52,568 --> 00:12:54,238
Electrified utes are getting cheaper,

257
00:12:54,288 --> 00:12:56,478
but most are still more
expensive up front,

258
00:12:56,528 --> 00:12:59,898
and they don't suit everyone especially
for heavy towing and long outback

259
00:12:59,948 --> 00:13:00,748
trips.

260
00:13:01,299 --> 00:13:02,789
And then there's the politics.

261
00:13:02,839 --> 00:13:05,769
Because the future of
these rules isn't settled.

262
00:13:05,819 --> 00:13:07,729
On the 29th of September 2026,

263
00:13:07,779 --> 00:13:12,249
the federal Coalition pledged to
repeal the NVES if it wins government.

264
00:13:12,299 --> 00:13:16,949
Shadow energy minister Dan Tehan
called it a "family car and ute tax",

265
00:13:16,999 --> 00:13:20,209
and said a repeal bill would be
introduced within thirty days of taking

266
00:13:20,259 --> 00:13:21,069
office.

267
00:13:21,119 --> 00:13:24,849
The Coalition argues the rules have
affected vehicle prices and choice,

268
00:13:24,899 --> 00:13:28,709
but carsales noted it hasn't put a
figure on how much repeal would reduce

269
00:13:28,759 --> 00:13:30,029
showroom prices.

270
00:13:30,079 --> 00:13:32,659
Supporters of the NVES
see it very differently.

271
00:13:32,709 --> 00:13:36,489
The Climate Council argued that
scrapping it would limit access to more

272
00:13:36,539 --> 00:13:40,139
efficient vehicles and increase
Australia's reliance on imported oil.

273
00:13:40,189 --> 00:13:43,749
Farmers for Climate Action said
repeal could reduce future choices for

274
00:13:43,799 --> 00:13:45,969
farmers, including electric utes.

275
00:13:46,019 --> 00:13:47,389
And the car industry?

276
00:13:47,439 --> 00:13:49,629
The Federal Chamber of
Automotive Industries,

277
00:13:49,679 --> 00:13:51,169
which represents car makers,

278
00:13:51,219 --> 00:13:52,369
said it needs "stable,

279
00:13:52,419 --> 00:13:55,989
predictable and workable policy settings"
because vehicle decisions are made

280
00:13:56,039 --> 00:13:57,209
years in advance.

281
00:13:57,259 --> 00:14:00,029
So right now, the NVES is law,

282
00:14:00,079 --> 00:14:02,949
it's under review, and the
opposition wants to scrap it.

283
00:14:02,999 --> 00:14:05,549
For ute buyers, that means uncertainty.

284
00:14:05,599 --> 00:14:09,309
Prices could rise in 2027 if
the targets stay as they are.

285
00:14:09,359 --> 00:14:11,549
The targets could be
softened by the review.

286
00:14:11,599 --> 00:14:15,429
Or the whole scheme could be repealed
after the next federal election.

287
00:14:15,479 --> 00:14:17,659
Nobody can tell you for
sure which way it'll go.

288
00:14:18,853 --> 00:14:21,803
So, what does all this mean if
you're planning to buy a ute?

289
00:14:21,853 --> 00:14:25,883
First, nobody has announced
a 2027 price rise yet.

290
00:14:25,933 --> 00:14:28,543
Toyota said it "cannot
rule out" increases.

291
00:14:28,593 --> 00:14:30,783
That's a warning, not a price list.

292
00:14:30,833 --> 00:14:33,023
Don't panic-buy because of a headline.

293
00:14:33,073 --> 00:14:36,323
Second, if you were already planning
to buy a diesel ute in the next few

294
00:14:36,373 --> 00:14:40,783
months, it's worth knowing that 2026
runout stock and year-end deals are on

295
00:14:40,833 --> 00:14:42,043
the table right now.

296
00:14:42,093 --> 00:14:44,323
If the price is right
and the ute suits you,

297
00:14:44,373 --> 00:14:46,523
there's no reason to wait for
things to get more expensive.

298
00:14:46,573 --> 00:14:49,663
Third, work out your real costs.

299
00:14:49,713 --> 00:14:52,503
With diesel prices where
they've been in 2026,

300
00:14:52,553 --> 00:14:56,403
a plug-in hybrid ute can save a lot on
fuel if you do lots of short trips and

301
00:14:56,453 --> 00:14:57,543
charge at home.

302
00:14:57,593 --> 00:14:59,863
But if you tow heavy loads long distances,

303
00:14:59,913 --> 00:15:03,803
check the real-world range and towing
figures very carefully before switching.

304
00:15:03,853 --> 00:15:07,683
And if you're thinking about a plug-in
hybrid ute through a novated lease,

305
00:15:07,733 --> 00:15:11,263
remember that plug-in hybrids lost their
fringe benefits tax exemption on the

306
00:15:11,313 --> 00:15:13,563
1st of April 2025.

307
00:15:13,613 --> 00:15:17,943
Only fully electric vehicles still qualify
and as we'll see in the next video,

308
00:15:17,993 --> 00:15:20,303
even that changes in 2027.

309
00:15:20,353 --> 00:15:21,703
If towing is your priority,

310
00:15:21,753 --> 00:15:24,803
compare the braked towing
capacity, not just the price.

311
00:15:24,853 --> 00:15:29,463
Some electrified utes now match diesel
on paper the MG U9 electric ute,

312
00:15:29,513 --> 00:15:33,323
for example, claims 3,500
kilograms of braked towing.

313
00:15:33,373 --> 00:15:35,283
But range drops a lot when you tow,

314
00:15:35,333 --> 00:15:38,083
so look for real-world
tests before you commit.

315
00:15:38,133 --> 00:15:40,263
Fourth, think about resale.

316
00:15:40,313 --> 00:15:42,043
If emissions rules keep tightening,

317
00:15:42,093 --> 00:15:45,223
the value of different types of utes
could change over the next few years.

318
00:15:45,273 --> 00:15:47,243
Nobody knows exactly how.

319
00:15:47,293 --> 00:15:50,723
But it's worth asking yourself what your
ute will be worth when you sell it in

320
00:15:50,773 --> 00:15:51,503
five years.

321
00:15:51,553 --> 00:15:55,743
And fifth, watch the NVES
review and the federal politics.

322
00:15:55,793 --> 00:15:56,803
If the targets are softened,

323
00:15:56,853 --> 00:16:00,603
or the scheme is repealed, the
pressure on ute prices could ease.

324
00:16:00,653 --> 00:16:04,113
If they stay, 2027 is when
the squeeze really starts.

325
00:16:05,007 --> 00:16:08,657
So, will ute prices rise
in Australia in 2027?

326
00:16:08,707 --> 00:16:10,217
Here's the honest answer.

327
00:16:10,267 --> 00:16:13,117
Toyota has openly warned
that it can't rule it out.

328
00:16:13,167 --> 00:16:19,097
The targets for utes drop from 180
grams to 150 grams in 2027 one of the

329
00:16:19,147 --> 00:16:21,337
biggest single-year jumps in the scheme.

330
00:16:21,387 --> 00:16:23,477
Most utes sold in Australia are diesel,

331
00:16:23,527 --> 00:16:25,697
and most of them are well above that line.

332
00:16:25,747 --> 00:16:29,197
And independent estimates suggest the
theoretical penalties could run into

333
00:16:29,247 --> 00:16:31,777
thousands of dollars per vehicle
by the end of the decade.

334
00:16:31,827 --> 00:16:34,937
And remember, it's not
only Toyota's problem.

335
00:16:34,987 --> 00:16:37,357
The Ranger, the D-Max, the Triton,

336
00:16:37,407 --> 00:16:41,177
the Navara and the BT-50 are
all mostly sold as diesels,

337
00:16:41,227 --> 00:16:44,857
and every one of those brands
faces the same 2027 target.

338
00:16:44,907 --> 00:16:45,897
But it's not a done deal.

339
00:16:45,947 --> 00:16:47,817
Car makers can trade credits,

340
00:16:47,867 --> 00:16:50,857
change their model mix, and
push more hybrids and plug-ins.

341
00:16:50,907 --> 00:16:52,517
The NVES is under review.

342
00:16:52,567 --> 00:16:54,937
And the opposition has
promised to scrap it.

343
